decision money-storage

context: We need to store and calculate monetary amounts throughout the application
decision: Money is always stored in cents as integers, never as floating point
rationale: Floating point arithmetic has precision errors. $0.10 + $0.20 != $0.30 in float. Financial calculations require exact precision.
enforcement: Money newtype must use int base. All monetary amounts are in cents.
examples:
    ✓ type Money = Money(int)
    ✓ charge(customer, Money(1000))  # $10.00
    ✗ type Money = Money(float)
    ✗ charge(customer, 10.00)
